Bad MmsNewCost conversion: 0
Insert errors: 220
Rows successfully inserted: 719
The 220 failures occur after MmsNewCost has already been successfully converted to 40877.75, 4971.08, etc.

So the problem is almost certainly another VARCHAR → NUMERIC conversion during the INSERT INTO SBCES.TempRbpCost.

Your current insert is:

INSERT INTO SBCES.TempRbpCost
VALUES
(
    @RebuiltStockNum,
    @TotalPrice,
    @DetailedDesc,
    @BuyNewCost,
    @Active,
    @Keyword
);

Because there is no column list, SQL Server relies on the physical column order of TempRbpCost. If its column order differs from these six variables, SQL Server can easily try to put something like @RebuiltStockNum or @DetailedDesc into a numeric column.

I would modify the procedure so the final output clearly tells us:

TOTAL ROWS
SUCCESSFUL
REJECTED
SOURCE CONVERSION ERRORS
INSERT ERRORS
ERROR REASON

And for every rejected row, it will print all six values being inserted, not just BuyNewCost.

